{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSBTQNke6AVgEmLjbRrN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job has been running every night; it just fails and then can't tell you. `launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`. The error log has the same two lines six times, and each line is one of the two bugs:\n\n1. **`Not logged in · Please run /login`**: launchd doesn't set `USER`, and your plist only sets `PATH`. Without `USER`, `claude` can't find its keychain login, so it exits 1 straight away. In your terminal `USER` is set, which is why it works by hand. **Fix:** I added `USER` = `vk` to the plist's `EnvironmentVariables`.\n2. **`nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status`**: in zsh, `status` is read-only, so `status=$?` stops the script before the failure notification. That's why you got silence instead of a FAILED message. It would also have blocked every success message, so fixing only the login would still have left you with nothing. **Fix:** I renamed it to `rc=$?`.\n\nI also made the script sturdier:\n- The prompt now goes to `claude` on stdin instead of as a multi-line argument.\n- A run that exits 0 but writes an empty summary is now reported as a failure.\n- Each run logs how long it took, `claude`'s exit code and the output size.\n- If `notify.sh` itself fails, that's written to the launchd log instead of disappearing.\n\nI tested the new script with stand-ins for `claude` and `notify.sh`: a failing run, an empty-output run and a successful run each sent the right message. I haven't run it under real launchd, Claude or Telegram.\n\n**To put the fix in place on your Mac**, reload the job and trigger a run. The plist only takes effect after a reload:\n\n```\nlaunchctl bootout gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review\nlaunchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist\nlaunchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review\n```\n\nThen check four things:\n- the exit code is 0\n- today's `nightly-review-<date>.md` exists and isn't empty\n- the run took tens of seconds, not one or two\n- the Telegram summary arrived\n\nThen break it once on purpose (for example, set `USER` to a wrong value) and make sure the FAILED message arrives.\n\n**From your colleague's note:** these parts applied:\n- checking `launchctl print` first\n- reading the error log before guessing\n- the zsh `status` bug\n- the `USER` fix for \"Not logged in\"\n- \"exit 0 doesn't prove it worked\"\n\nTheir \"Input must be provided\" prompt-argument failure isn't in your log; I switched the prompt to stdin anyway as a precaution. With the prompt on stdin, `< /dev/null` isn't needed. The rest (their schedule, the correction history, the linked article) didn't apply. ANSWER.md has the full breakdown."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1954,"cache_read_input_tokens":27014,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1954},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72faa24f-f44c-4e4b-ba0b-93ce24187db9","uuid":"9e17e6e1-642f-42b8-834d-5614e2e4c5b8","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:22:00.073Z","request_id":"req_011CgSBTQ59o63xjdSSvyzo9"}
